## Later milestones

After actual production access: validate real routes across North America, Europe and Japan; booking-price match, taxes/baggage, missing airline coverage and latency. Confirm redistribution/attribution before activating revenue claims. Add manually vetted airport gateways and resort transfer pages, hotels/cars APIs, separate local arrival/check-in dates, and a trip-cost breakdown only when components are quoted. Consider saved plans, shareable itineraries and paid alerts after accuracy is proven. Do not query all resorts on every heatmap hover. Group shared airports; cache only as licensed.

## Research decisions to retain

Google has supplier integrations, no open consumer Google Flights search API. SerpApi is third-party scraping, not Google authorization or affiliate income. Skyscanner API gate is 100K MAU; its affiliate gate is >5K monthly unique visitors. Aviasales live API gate is 50K MAU and disallows mixing competing metasearch APIs; its cached Data API is inappropriate as live storm-trip pricing. Amadeus self-service is decommissioned. Duffel is a ticket-selling model with fees, not the first click-out affiliate choice. Expedia and DiscoverCars remain possible later affiliate candidates. Recheck terms before integration.

