## Phase 2 — 2026-11-06

Implemented a separate native-dialog Compare trips view, reachable from the header or the existing three-resort comparison. Shared preferences include departure airport, departure/arrival/ski/return dates, adults, currency, optional budget, pass and ground-travel preference. A single plan, its three resorts and chosen arrival airports can be saved in localStorage and reopened on the same browser. This is device storage, not a profile or cross-device account.

Comparison shows snow only for complete, fresh forecast coverage of the actual ski dates. It attempts a live forecast refresh for selected resorts when coverage is missing, reports failures, and preserves unknown operations. It displays pass catalog membership with a restrictions reminder, unquoted trip costs, airport selectors, KAYAK search links and directions/lodging discovery. Budget is stored as a target; no price matching or cost ranking is claimed. Date changes invalidate the displayed comparison until Update comparison is clicked. Duplicate resorts are rejected.

Official gateway references verified Nov 6:
- Whistler/YVR: https://www.yvr.ca/en/passengers/transportation/public-transportation/long-distance-scheduled-buses/whistler
- Heavenly/RNO: https://www.skiheavenly.com/Explore%20the%20Resort/About%20the%20Resort/Getting%20Here%20and%20Parking.aspx
- Niseko/CTS: https://www.niseko.ne.jp/en/getting-to-niseko3/
- Chamonix/GVA: https://en.chamonix.com/usual-information-services/transports
These identify access airports and official planning pages, not verified service availability for a user's exact dates. Other resorts retain explicitly geographic suggestions. No schedules, prices, driving times or ski-bag policies invented.

New modules: js/trip-planning.js (pure logic, gateway references), js/trip-comparison.js (dialog and storage). Integration in main.js, comparison.js, travel-panel.js and detail-panel.js; styling in travel.css. New tests in tests/trip-planning.test.mjs.

Validation: 68 Node tests and 13 Python tests passed, including static packaging. Browser verified three cards, fresh live model totals, duplicate rejection, successful save and reload, valid outgoing search links, and 390px mobile dialog with equal scroll/client widths (350px; no horizontal overflow). Screenshot: output/travel-build-qa/comparison.png. Local preview uses TRAVEL_PORT=4176 node server/travel-server.mjs; open http://127.0.0.1:4176/ and click Compare trips. Default port 4174 remains supported. Restart server after edits because its public assets are packaged at startup.

The local stored conditions snapshot was stale during QA, so operations correctly remained unverified; live model requests subsequently supplied ski-window snowfall. This build does not repair scheduled snapshot collection. Production fares, budget-based recommendations, flight-arrival matching, transfer availability, multi-device profiles and alerts remain future work. KAYAK credentials are still required for API prices. Changes are local and have not been pushed or deployed.

### Date-entry refinement — Nov 6
Grouped all five dates into three numbered fieldsets: Getting there (flight from home departs, flight arrives at destination), Your ski days (first/last day skiing), Heading home (flight home departs). Helper text identifies the airport/resort whose local calendar applies. Other preferences now follow the date groups. Existing field names and saved plans remain compatible. Desktop uses three columns; mobile stacks the journey stages. Verified at 390px without horizontal overflow, ran the three trip-planning tests and all 13 Python/packaging tests; syntax and diff checks passed. Screenshot: output/travel-build-qa/date-groups.png. Local preview restarted on 4176; not deployed.

### Two-date simplification — Nov 6
Supersedes the five-date layout above. Only Depart from home and Return flight date are required. Arrival date removed. Set my ski days is an optional checkbox revealing first/last ski days; it is off for new and legacy saved plans unless explicitly enabled. Validation requires both ski dates only when enabled and bounds them within travel dates. With custom dates off, cards show available fresh daily forecast values within the travel window, with explicit partial-coverage wording and no personalized ski-trip total. Existing saved optional values remain available without being applied silently.
Validated four trip-planning tests plus 13 Python/packaging tests, syntax and diff checks; desktop mouse/keyboard toggle, daily forecast mode, two visible/required date fields, and 390px mobile without horizontal overflow. Screenshot: output/travel-build-qa/two-dates.png. Local preview restarted on 4176. Not deployed.

### Popup layout refinement — Nov 6
Reorganized the existing comparison dialog: compact home-airport/adults/travel-dates row, clearly grouped resort selectors, optional details disclosure for ski days/pass/transport/budget/currency, and comparison cards below. Header and footer remain visible while the middle content scrolls. Save and Compare buttons remain functional in the footer through native form association. Close uses the existing x.svg icon. Dialog dimensions stay stable when results clear; the global page keyboard handler defers to the native dialog for focus/Escape.

Verified desktop and 390px mobile layouts, no horizontal body overflow (350px client/scroll width), preference disclosure and custom-day toggle, external-footer form submission generating three cards, successful save, and Escape dismissal. Screenshots: output/travel-build-qa/refined-popup.png. Final checks: 69 Node tests and 13 Python tests passed, JS syntax and git diff checks passed. Local only; no deployment.


