Priority sequence:
1. Connect approved KAYAK production access behind a private backend; validate fares, actual arrival timing, baggage and returned tracked booking links.
2. Apply for Expedia Group Travel Creator Program as the first accommodation affiliate candidate, then Booking.com via its official regional affiliate-network route. Evaluate Agoda specifically against Japan routes. Affiliate approval does not automatically grant live hotel-search API access: confirm that separately.
3. Benchmark actual ski-area inventory, final tax-inclusive prices, cancellation, mobile handoff, date/occupancy preservation, attribution and completed-stay earnings. Do not pick providers by advertised commission alone.
4. Match lodging to resort/lifts or a usable shuttle, using actual local arrival/check-in dates once known. Preserve a direct property option and map discovery when those benefit the traveler, regardless of affiliate eligibility. Disclose commissions, avoid forced redirects/popunders, and never invent referral identifiers or live rates.
5. Expand verified transfer operators, timetables, pickup/return locations and ski-bag capacity for a small initial gateway set; add suitable rental referrals. No invented winter travel times.
6. Add licensed caching, provider request budgets, server-side secrets, monitoring of failed/limited requests and stale-price withholding.
7. Track outbound search/booking clicks and reconcile with partner reports for completed bookings, cancellations, net commissions and payout timing. Income remains unproven until sufficient real conversion data exists.

Accommodation sources checked Nov 6:
- https://partner.expediagroup.com/en-us/solutions/build-your-travel-experience/travel-creator-program : up to 4% on eligible transactions, current product rates inside account; Expedia/Hotels.com/Vrbo. No assumption that every booking earns the advertised maximum.
- https://help.creator.expediagroup.com/hc/en-us/articles/15187327581591-What-commission-will-I-earn : actual rates vary by travel product.
- https://www.booking.com/affiliate-program/v2/index.html : official affiliate-network registration; displayed English/US route directs to CJ. Region/acceptance and commission terms must be confirmed, no percentage assumed.
- https://partners.agoda.com/tl-ph/faq.html : progressive model advertised up to 7%; contractual/account rate and payout conditions need verification before financial modeling. Japan inventory superiority is a hypothesis to test, not a verified outcome.

User-benefit rule: affiliate links are acceptable when they lead to a competitive, suitable offer. Ranking must reflect location, final cost, cancellation and traveler needs. Include better non-affiliate/direct booking options when available. A map is useful for location discovery; it does not itself guarantee better booking prices or fund the site.

### OpenWeather incident / usage control priority

Nick received a temporary-block email reporting repeated breaches of 60 requests/minute. Investigation found OpenWeather used only by cloud/precipitation/temperature tile overlays in js/weather-layers.js, shared by globe and mountain views. Open-Meteo supplies resort weather/7-day model forecasts; RainViewer supplies radar; resort adapters supply operational reports. Historical snowfall is modeled/reanalysis data, not OpenWeather.

Each OpenWeather tile image is a separate request. Provider cache is per viewer and does not enforce account-wide requests/minute. Existing pending-layer deduplication and maximum zoom 6 limit some load but do not establish a quota. Layer activation also makes a validation tile request. No shared rate limiter, cross-user cache or account-wide 429 circuit breaker exists. Provider error handler displays an error but does not remove offending layers. Panning/zooming, simultaneous layers and multiple tabs/users can therefore create bursts. This is a plausible source of the block, not proof of the historical usage counts; provider logs/account records are needed to attribute exact traffic. No test calls were sent to the blocked OpenWeather key in this audit.

Remediation to implement before resuming/scaling overlays: pause affected overlay use; add account-wide request governance and explicit stop/backoff on authentication/quota failures, deduplicate/cache only as permitted, isolate optional map-layer failures from core weather, retain attribution, inspect provider usage records, and resume only once within the plan. Do not recommend a paid upgrade merely to conceal uncontrolled requests. Local git-ignored key configuration does not constitute secrecy for browser tile URLs. Backend/credential and deployment-path review needed. Static packaging currently excludes data/config.json, so do not assume the current public Pages build is using the local key without checking the actual deployed artifact.

Provider horizon/license findings:
- OpenWeather free forecast is 5 days at 3-hour steps: https://openweathermap.org/api/forecast5
- One Call 3.0 has 8-day daily forecasts, separate subscription: https://openweathermap.org/api/one-call-3
- 16-day daily forecast appears on paid weather plans: https://openweathermap.org/price . Existing map tiles are not those forecasts.
- Snow Scout currently requests forecast_days=7 from Open-Meteo. Open-Meteo documents up to 16 days, depending on model support: https://open-meteo.com/en/docs . Longer horizon is not equivalent to reliable exact snowfall.
- https://open-meteo.com/en/pricing : commercial API access requires a paid commercial license; free access is for evaluation/non-commercial use. Plan this before affiliate monetization. Historical/reanalysis availability may need a different plan from forecast access. Data attribution obligations remain.
- RainViewer commercial-use and caching rights need a separate check before monetization; do not assume public API access licenses commercial use.

Recommendation: retain current Open-Meteo model pipeline as the main forecast source with appropriate commercial access; treat OpenWeather overlays as an optional separately budgeted map service. Fix usage controls before choosing paid OpenWeather versus a licensed replacement tile provider. No weather code, provider subscription or live deployment was changed in this research/plan update.

### OpenWeather request-control fix — Nov 6
Implemented the first controlled weather gateway and removed direct browser access to the key. See docs/weather-request-controls.md for the full request path, tests, rollout boundary and reactivation instructions. OpenWeather remains explicitly paused in the local preview while the account is blocked. Rolling maximum: 45 upstream attempts per minute per gateway process, shared by all its clients/layers, with in-flight deduplication, startup drain, quota/auth circuit breakers and no automatic retries. Browser tile errors remove affected layers and stop retrying; radar stays independent. No subscription changed, blocked-key calls made or deployment performed. 77 Node + 13 Python tests passed. Public multi-instance hosting requires central persistent state before enabling the key. Close/reload any tabs running the older direct-tile code.

### Public controlled backend — Nov 6
Cloudflare weather backend deployed at https://snow-scout-weather.nick-naugle.workers.dev with a SQLite Durable Object for persistent shared reservations/circuit state; frontend weather-config points to that service. Existing Free plan used, no account upgrade. Service is live but provider calls remain disabled. Key transfer was rejected by automatic approval review pending specific user consent; no key was uploaded. See worker/README.md for deployment and activation instructions. KAYAK/hotel endpoints are not claimed as deployed by this weather-backend release.
